/* book: lead: An autopilot closes the control loop automatically. Sensors measure the aircraft's actual attitude, rate or path. A computer compares that with the commanded value and sends a correction. Servos move the surfaces or the throttles. The pilot selects a mode and a target; the machine holds it. This frees attention for navigation and monitoring, and it is the basis of every automatic flight control sy */
