/* book Worked example 2: Q: Heading select: the outer loop commands bank φc = 1.0 × heading error, limited to 25°. The aircraft flies at 120 m/s on heading 070° and the pilot selects 110°. (a) Find the bank command. (b) Find the turn rate at 25° of bank, with g = 9.81 m/s². (c) Estimate how long the bank stays at the 25° limit, ignoring roll-in time.
   1. (a) Heading error = 110° − 070° = 40° (turn right). Unlimited command = 1.0 × 40 = 40°, above the limit, so φc = 25° right. The inner roll loop of worked example 1 then flies the aircraft to that bank.
   2. (b) In a level coordinated turn, turn rate ω = g tan φ ÷ V = 9.81 × tan 25° ÷ 120 = 9.81 × 0.4663 ÷ 120 = 0.0381 rad/s = 2.18°/s.
   3. (c) The command stays at the limit until the error falls to 25°, that is for 40° − 25° = 15° of turn: 15 ÷ 2.18 = 6.9 s. After that the bank command shrinks with the error and the aircraft rolls out smoothly on 110°.
   Answer: The bank command is limited to 25° right; the turn rate is 2.18°/s; the bank stays at 25° for about 6.9 s, then the outer loop reduces it as the heading error closes. */
