/* book exam traps: The auto-throttle moves thrust levers only; it never commands pitch. Saying it controls altitude is wrong unless the autopilot pitch channel is also engaged. | An autopilot without servos is only a computer. The servo is the part that moves the surface or lever. | Getting the rate-feedback sign wrong. With e and p both positive to the right, δ = Kp e − Kr p: rolling toward the target cuts the command, rolling away (p negative) adds to it. The wrong sign removes damping and increases overshoot. | A single-axis wing leveller holds wings level; it does not hold altitude or heading by itself. | Approach Category I, II or III is set by decision height and runway visual range, not by the number of autopilot channels alone. */
